BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairlocal": "https://montclairlocal.news/event/food-tour-and-history-walk-of-montclair/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairlocal
X-SOURCE:Montclair Local News
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T160000
DTSTAMP:20260816T174354Z
CREATED:20260816T174354Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260816T174354Z
UID:10141242-1787403600-1787414400@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:Food Tour and History Walk of Montclair
DESCRIPTION:Explore Montclair\, NJ on this immersive food tour showcasing a hyperlocal culinary hotspot\, co-hosted by Chow Town Food Tours and Montclair History Center. \n“Montclair In Motion” is a social\, flavorful experience rooted in this colorful community’s unique industrial history and more recent cultural growth\, including culinary traditions from Argentina\, the Philippines\, Sicily\, West Africa\, and Brazil. \nChow Town Food Tours and the Montclair History Center will provide expert insights for a tour to remember. This guided exploration of Bloomfield Avenue will lead guests on a leisurely one-mile walk\, stopping for Brazilian comfort food\, humongous cookies\, and more. Meet the chefs and business owners that make this one of the most exciting restaurant scenes in the state. \nDiscover the hidden history behind architecture\, landmarks\, and other notable highlights from the experts at the nonprofit Montclair History Center. \nBring an appetite! The tour will visit several fantastic NJ eateries\, including unapologetic Jersey pizza\, Calabrian-style; international fusion cuisine with a twist from Montclair locals; Brazilian homestyle fare from a lauded cookbook author; a slinger of humongous\, addictive cookies; and more! \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/food-tour-and-history-walk-of-montclair/
LOCATION:Crane Park\, Montclair\, NJ
CATEGORIES:Food
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Chow-Town-Food-Tour-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Thespaceforart": "https://thespaceforart.com/event/assemblage-lab-gallery-talk-with-andrew-borg/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:thespaceforart
X-SOURCE:The Space For Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T150000
DTSTAMP:20260729T184955Z
CREATED:20260729T184955Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T184955Z
UID:10015-1787403600-1787410800@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Assemblage Lab & Gallery Talk with Andrew Borg
DESCRIPTION:Assemblage Lab & Gallery Talk with Andrew Borg\nClosing Event for “Unrecyclable: Look Again” \nWhat do you see when you really look at what you throw away? \nJoin artist Andrew Borg for the closing event of Unrecyclable: Look Again — an afternoon that begins with a gallery talk and ends with your hands deep in materials you never thought twice about discarding. \nAfter walking through the exhibition and sharing the story behind his two-year collection of unrecyclable plastics\, foams\, and composites\, Borg leads an immersive hands-on Assemblage Lab in which participants get to experience the process firsthand. Using unrecyclable packaging\, abandoned electronics\, appliances\, and other “ghost objects\,” you’ll build your own assemblage\, sculpture\, or mixed-media artwork — guided by the same impulse that drove this exhibition: look again. \nNo artistic experience required. No right or wrong. Just a fresh set of eyes and a willingness to see the overlooked as raw material for something new. \nUnrecyclable materials are provided\, along with glue to put your assemblages together. Bring your own materials too — packaging\, foam inserts\, bottle caps\, old electronics\, anything you’ve been meaning to throw away. The stranger the better. \n🗓 Saturday\, August 22 | 1:00 pm – 3:00 pm\n📍 The Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, 2nd Floor\, Montclair\, NJ\n🎟 $10 \nPart gallery talk\, part art lab\, all creative. Come ready to make something!
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/assemblage-lab-gallery-talk-with-andrew-borg/
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-29-at-2.48.27-PM.png
END:VEVENT
