X-SOURCE:Meetup: Board Game Night at Verona Inn
UID:event_rtxzvtyjclbjc@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260822T020940Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260826T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260826T213000
SUMMARY:Meeting at the Verona inn!
DESCRIPTION:Board Game Night At Verona Inn\nWe will be doing our first mon
 thly meeting starting on **February 25th at the Verona Inn!** We will be m
 eeting up to organize games starting at 7:30\, with food and drinks availa
 ble courtesy of our host! You can play any game provided by hosts or bring
  your own! If you do not have a friend group to play games\, hosts will or
 ganize you into pods with other people who need players. There are **no du
 es**. Future meetings will be held on the **last Wednesday of each month.*
 *\n\nMore information and ground rules:\n\n* **The doors open at 6:30 but 
 games do not start until 7:30.** I *highly recommend* coming in during thi
 s period to eat your food and drink ahead of time!\n* **Please return the 
 graciousness provided by our hosts and order at least one item! All venue 
 specific rules apply to our club.** Future meetings depend on treating our
  hosts with respect.\n* **All games must be returned to their owners when 
 they announce that they are leaving.** If you are in a game in progress wh
 en the meeting ends but it is not borrowed you may continue playing!\n* **
 Please place food and drink on a separate table or surface from your games
 ** to help avoid stains and other damage.\n* **Please engage with others i
 n good faith\, sportsmanship\, respect and common sense.** *ABSOLUTELY NO 
 harassment\, getting physical\, hurtful insulting\, and persecutory langua
 ge will be tolerated.* Repeat violators of venue rules AND/OR this rule ma
 y be asked to leave the event and not return.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/board-game-night-at-verona-inn/events
 /rtxzvtyjclbjc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260209T235401Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260209T235401Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Campuslabs Montclair": "https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539150"}
X-SOURCE-ID:campuslabs_montclair
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Weeks of Welcome
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFinding Your Civic Voice. Your Voice H
 as Power. Come learn wow to use it.\nKick off the semester by discovering
  the power of your voice! As part of Weeks of Welcome\, Civic and Voter E
 ngagement invites you to Finding Your Civic Voice\, an interactive worksh
 op designed to help you connect your passions with meaningful civic actio
 n.\nThrough engaging activities and guided discussion\, you'll explore wh
 at civic voice means\, reflect on the issues that matter most to you\, an
 d identify how your unique experiences and perspectives can make a differ
 ence. Whether you're passionate about education\, the environment\, menta
 l health\, social justice\, or another cause\, this workshop will help yo
 u transform your ideas into action.\nTogether\, we'll explore how everyda
 y actions—such as voting\, volunteering\, advocating\, or engaging in res
 pectful dialogue—can strengthen your community and create lasting impact.
  You'll also learn how to communicate your perspective in a clear and mea
 ningful way while developing an achievable next step to stay involved thr
 oughout your time at Montclair State.\nParticipants will:\n\nExplore what
  civic voice is and why it matters\nIdentify an issue they're passionate 
 about\nDevelop a concise message that reflects their values and experienc
 es\nLeave with a practical action plan to begin making a difference\n\nWh
 ether you're new to civic engagement or already involved\, this workshop 
 is a great opportunity to meet fellow students\, share ideas\, and start 
 the year with purpose. Join us during Weeks of Welcome and discover how y
 our voice can help shape both our campus and our communities.\n\n\n\n\n\n
  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nHosted by: Civic & Voter Engagement\, O
 ffice of Student Belonging\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: htt
 ps://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539150
