X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10341
DTSTART:20260827T223000Z
DTEND:20260827T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260827T000000Z
SUMMARY:Family History: Through Historical Research and Genealogy
DESCRIPTION:Information\n\nA method that takes an investigative approach to 
 the study of family history and genealogy. In this presentation\, you will 
 hear from a historian who has 25 years of experience doing investigations 
 on innovative approaches to genealogy and how to think differently. There 
 is a wide range of topics that can be covered in this course\, ranging from 
 the foundations of using Ancestry and establishing a family tree to more 
 advanced topics such as overcoming brick walls and delving deeper into 
 historical and genealogical material.\n\nAbout the presenter\n\n\n	James 
 Calaski completed his undergraduate studies at William Paterson University 
 of New Jersey in 1998.\n	He served with the Glen Rock\, New Jersey\, Police 
 Department for over twenty years\, earning numerous awards and 
 citations.\n	He later earned a Master of Arts in History from William 
 Paterson University of New Jersey in May 2013.\n\n\nThis program will be 
 held in Community Room 1.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-16888674
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16888674
END:VEVENT
