X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ics Kstx8Swyw669Kakgqa 6478083 Ics": "https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2131910341"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ics_kstx8swyw669kakgqa_6478083_ics
SUMMARY:Selichot - Service\, Dinner\, Music!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T213000
DTSTAMP:20260820T020055Z
UID:TU2131910341
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T183000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260714T210247Z
DESCRIPTION:Start the High Holidays with joy\, music and community! Join u
 s for a lively evening packed with delicious food\, soulful singing and sw
 eet treats. Connect with the Shomrei community over dinner and sing High H
 oliday melodies. Unwind with dessert and smooth sounds from our jazz band.
  It’s a celebration you won’t want to miss!\n\n**RSVP Required for Din
 ner and Reception** **http://shomrei.org/jazz**: http://shomrei.org/jazz\n
 \nFree or Suggested Donation:  \n$20 per adult\, $10 per child over 12\, $
 36 per family\n\n**------------------------------  \nAdults and Kids 8+ (Y
 ounger Kids/Scroll Down)**  \n6:30 Welcome   \n6:45 Dinner (Middle Eastern
  dairy dinner)  \n8:00 Havdalah and Selichot Service  \n9:00 Dessert and J
 azz Reception\n\nAs Shabbat comes to a close\, children and adults will co
 me together to recite Havdalah prayers. We are looking forward to having o
 ur children who are 8 yrs old and up help lead the havdalah candle lightin
 g ceremony while reciting prayers with Rabbi Julie.\n\nParticipatory\, mus
 ic-filled service led by Rabbi Julie\, Talia Lakritz\, Suzanna Grobman\, D
 ebra Caplan and accompanied by Oren Neiman and his jazz ensemble.\n\nThe p
 arty continues with a dessert reception. Live music will be provided by th
 e jazz ensemble.\n\n**Livestream:** http://shomrei.org/live\n\n**---------
 ---------------------**\n\n**Kids 7 and Younger**  \n6:30 Little Kids' Din
 ner   \n7:00 Free Play  \n7:30 Selichot Inspired Art Activity  \n8:00 Chil
 dren welcome to stay in childcare\, or join Selichot service\n\n**--------
 ----------------------**\n\n**Have questions? Want to Help out? Contact:**
  Shomrei Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(973) 746-5031\n\n**What is Selic
 hot?**  \nThe Hebrew word selichah means “forgiveness.” The plural for
 m of the word selichah is selichot\, a word traditionally used to refer to
  additional prayers for forgiveness recited during the month of Elul (thro
 ugh Yom Kippur). We gather together on the Saturday night before Rosh Hash
 anah to meditate on the capacity for forgiveness and on its power. In join
 ing together\, we help each other pray for that blessing – to give it an
 d to receive it.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260807T215954Z
LOCATION:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2131910341
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
X-TEAMUP-ROOM:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah
END:VEVENT
